<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= @page.language_code %>">
  <head>
    <%= render "laiss_cms/pages/meta_data" %>
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <%#
      This layout is written into your application by the install generator, as a
      starting point. It references `application`, the layout and asset name Rails
      generates by default.

      It deliberately loads NOTHING from a remote host. An earlier version of this
      file pulled Tailwind from a CDN with a <script src>, which meant every
      public page made a third-party request — a dependency on someone else's
      uptime, a privacy problem, and a surprise for anyone reading the network tab.

      If you want Tailwind, install it properly:

        bin/rails tailwindcss:install

      ...which compiles it locally into your own asset pipeline.
    %>

    <%# `stylesheet_link_tag 'application'` is a no-op when the host app has no
        application.css, and Rails raises in strict mode, so this is guarded. %>
    <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", media: "all", "data-turbo-track": "reload" rescue nil %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" rescue nil %>
  </head>

  <body>
    <%= yield %>
    <%= render "laiss_cms/edit_mode" %>
  </body>
</html>
